itions like pancreatic cancer and cirrhosis.\n\nPatients may require adjustments to their insulin dosages based on their individual needs, and monitoring is essential to ensure effective management of their blood glucose levels. Insulin can also be included in parenteral nutrition protocols when necessary. However, some patients may struggle with adherence to their insulin regimen, leading to omitted doses, which can complicate their diabetes management.\n\nOverall, insulin is a fundamental medication in the treatment of diabetes, helping to regulate glucose metabolism and maintain health in individuals with this chronic condition.\",33\r\n4190,CETOACIDOSIS,\"Cetoacidosis is a serious metabolic condition primarily associated with diabetes, particularly diabetic ketoacidosis, which occurs when the body produces high levels of ketones due to insufficient insulin. This condition can lead to elevated blood sugar levels and is a significant complication for individuals with diabetes. Additionally, ketoacidosis can also occur in adults with Maple Syrup Urine Disease, often triggered by intercurrent illnesses. Overall, cetoacidosis is characterized by the body's excessive production of ketones, making it a critical health concern that requires prompt medical attention.\",11\r\n2303,PACIENTES QUEMADOS,\"\"\"PACIENTES QUEMADOS\"\" refers to individuals who have suffered from burns and require specialized nutritional management due to their hypermetabolic and catabolic responses following the injury. These patients are particularly vulnerable, as they often experience critical burn injuries that place them at a high risk of malnutrition. Their condition is characterized by hypermetabolism, hypercatabolism, and inflammation, necessitating careful dietary interventions to support their recovery and overall health.\",25\r\n144,FÁRMACOS,\"Fármacos, or drugs and medications, are substances utilized in the treatment of various medical conditions. They play a crucial role in clinical practice, particularly in their interactions with diet and nutrients, which can significantly affect their efficacy and absorption. Fármacos may need to be administered to patients receiving enteral nutrition, necessitating specific guidelines to ensure proper delivery and effectiveness.\n\nCertain medications, such as antibiotics and laxatives, are commonly associated with gastrointestinal side effects, including diarrhea and constipation. Additionally, fármacos like somatostatin analogs are specifically used to manage dumping syndrome and its related symptoms. The gastrointestinal side effects of fármacos can vary widely, with some causing chronic diarrhea depending on their nature and usage.\n\nFármacos are also essential in the control of metabolic processes, particularly in patients with burns, where they assist in managing nutrimetabolic needs. Furthermore, these medications can interact with nutrients during nutritional therapy, potentially impacting treatment outcomes. They may also affect thermoregulation and hydration in athletes, highlighting the importance of understanding their interactions with dietary components.\n\nMoreover, certain medications can interfere with swallowing functionality, especially in the elderly, and can disrupt the absorption and metabolism of thyroid hormones, which may compromise treatment efficacy. Overall, fármacos encompass a wide range of medications that require careful consideration of their interactions with diet and nutrients to optimize patient care.\",18\r\n14199,INTERACCIONES,\"INTERACCIONES refers to the interactions between drugs and diet, as well as between drugs and nutrients, which are significant in clinical settings and can affect treatment outcomes. These interactions are particularly relevant in nutritional therapy and must be considered to avoid adverse effects. Understanding these interacciones is crucial for optimizing treatment efficacy and ensuring patient safety.\",3\r\n2375,FÓRMULAS NUTRICIONALES,\"FÓRMULAS NUTRICIONALES refers to specialized nutritional formulas that serve multiple purposes in dietary management. These formulas can be utilized to establish nutritional requirements in situations where indirect calorimetry is not available. Additionally, they are specifically designed for diabetic patients, incorporating modified carbohydrates and an increased fat content to better meet their dietary needs.\",2\r\n3084,HORMONA DEL CRECIMIENTO,\"The \"\"HORMONA DEL CRECIMIENTO,\"\" or growth hormone (GH), is a crucial hormone produced by the pituitary gland that plays a significant role in stimulating growth, cell reproduction, and regeneration in humans and other animals. It is essential for muscle and tissue growth, and its decline with age can lead to frailty and a loss of muscle mass. In specific medical contexts, such as in patients with Turner syndrome, GH is secreted to enhance adult height, although its effectiveness may vary based on multiple factors.\n\nAdditionally, growth hormone regulates both growth and metabolism, and an excess of this hormone can result in conditions such as acromegaly. GH is also utilized in the treatment of patients with severe burns, as it aids in reducing healing time and associated costs. During pregnancy, the growth hormone secreted by the placenta increases levels of insulin-like growth factor 1 (IGF-1), further highlighting its importance in various physiological processes.\",9\r\n4261,BETABLOQUEANTES,\"Beta-blockers, known as \"\"BETABLOQUEANTES,\"\" are a class of medications primarily used to manage various heart conditions, including acute coronary syndrome. They are particularly recommended for diabetic patients due to their beneficial effects on cardiovascular health. In critical care settings, these drugs are considered essential for managing patients' conditions effectively. Additionally, specific beta-blockers, such as propranolol and metoprolol, are utilized in burn patients to reduce muscle catabolism and enhance immune response, highlighting their versatility in treating different medical scenarios.\",4\r\n5354,OXANDROLONA,\"OXANDROLONA es un fármaco que se utiliza en el contexto del tratamiento de pacientes críticos. Se trata de un derivado sintético de la testosterona, que se emplea especialmente en adultos que sufren de quemaduras severas, con el objetivo de aumentar la masa magra y acelerar la cicatrización de heridas. Además, la oxandrolona es un tratamiento recomendado para pacientes con síndrome de Turner que han comenzado el tratamiento con hormona de crecimiento de manera tardía y que presentan un pronóstico de talla final insatisfactorio.\",4\r\n4165,CADENCIAS DE INSULINA,Insulin pulses refer to the rhythmic release of insulin from beta cells in response to glucose levels.,1\r\n4161,CÁLCIO,\"Calcium is a chemical element that plays a crucial role in various cellular processes, including muscle contraction and neurotransmitter release.\",1\r\n4049,PRUEBA FUNCIONAL,\"Prueba funcional refers to dynamic functional tests used to evaluate the reserve of the pituitary gland, particularly in assessing hormonal deficiencies.\",1\r\n2313,HIPOVOLEMIA,,1\r\n14341,SORBITO,,1\r\n5540,PLACENTA,The placenta is an organ that provides nutrients and oxygen to the fetus and secretes hormones during pregnancy.,1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n3183,PACIENTE,INSULINA,\"The patient has been receiving insulin as a critical part of their treatment for Type 1 diabetes, aimed at controlling elevated blood glucose levels. Following their diabetes diagnosis, the patient's insulin levels were adjusted to better manage their condition. It is essential for the patient to adjust their insulin dosage based on their carbohydrate intake to maintain optimal glucose control. However, it has been noted that the patient has been omitting doses of insulin, which may impact their overall management of diabetes.\",579\r\n3264,PACIENTE,CETOACI